There are two sorts of poison; being deadly poisoned (getting "ill") is
from corpses that got too old, or from inherently old corpses like undead
creatures (zombies, etc.). Generally avoid those corpses. And there are
poisonous corpses that are not good for your health (and can kill you if
your constitution is bad and your HPs too low); avoid those corpses, too.
(BTW, for the latter kind of poisoning there is also a certain amulet and
a certain ring that protects you.)

Memorize what corpse was healthy in one game and you'll learn quickly for
the future!

The mines, a branch that starts somewhere between level 2 and 4 with a
second staircase down, has many inhabitants whose corpses you can eat.
Don't eat the kobolds.

You can always eat food rations, there's no aging. (But sometimes you'll
have temporary "difficulties" eating; don't get repelled by that.)

If you got "ill" from food or are "weak" from hunger and have nothing to
eat then pray. But don't pray too often.

